  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposed extension of the back addition eaves and roof terrace over the back addition, by reason of their scale, design and location, would result in a dominant and unsympathetic addition to the harm of the character and appearance of the host building and local visual amenity. The development would therefore fail to comply with the NPPF (2024), policies LP1 and LP5 of the Wandsworth Local Plan (2023) and the guidance of the Housing SPD (2016).\r\n",
    "Reason : 2 - The extension of the back addition eaves and roof terrace over the back addition, by reason of their siting, scale and design would constitute an unneighbourly form of development that would harm the amenity of the neighbouring property in the form of loss of outlook, being overbearing and creating an increased sense of enclosure. The application has also failed to demonstrate that there would not be unacceptable harm to neighbouring windows in respect to reductions in daylight. The development would therefore fail to comply with policy LP2 of the Wandsworth Local Plan (2023) and the guidance of the Housing SPD (2016).\r\n",
    "Reason : 3 - In dealing with this application the Council has implemented the requirement in the National Planning Policy Framework to work with the applicant in a positive and proactive manner and the Council has, as far as practicable, sought solutions to problems arising in relation to dealing with the planning application. We have made available detailed advice in the form of our statutory policies in the Local Plan, Supplementary Planning documents and where appropriate the Site Specific Allocations Document as well as offering a full pre application advice service. However, we have been unable to seek solutions to problems as the proposal is clearly contrary to our statutory policies and negotiation could not overcome the reasons for refusal."
  ],
